      "reason": "with no other model jobs on the machine (the first run overlapped other agents' model tests); predictions were identical row for row",
      "note": "LoRA label-only p95 is noisy on this laptop even without other model jobs: 1108 ms in the first run, 1392 ms in the re-run, 945 ms in a separate in-process pass, while p50 was 97-110 ms in both benchmark runs. Slow rows skew longer but length does not explain them alone (a 49-character command took 2.6 s), and other model jobs do not explain the tail; it was not investigated further. Rules commits after the re-measure (fc764d8, de241bd) change three rows: `git add aws-credentials.csv` (row 10) now blocks as labelled, and two `git add` of OAuth private keys (rows 78, 184) are now blocked by a rule instead of the model. With those rules, rules-only would score 59.3% and the full engine 87.0%; the table keeps the measured values."
    }
